    // ---- fields the layouts gained from the engine's own field table ----
    // Naming a field only makes it readable. It reaches a definition when it is paired with an
    // entry here, and these are the pairings where the target uses the same word the engine does,
    // give or take the capitals. Nothing is inferred beyond that: a field whose name has no
    // counterpart is left unmapped rather than guessed at.

